{% endif %}## Install

```sh
curl -fsSLo ~/.config/tmux/acid-acetic.conf \
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/acid-theme/tmux/main/acid-acetic.conf
```

Source it from `tmux.conf`, above the local settings:

```tmux
source-file ~/.config/tmux/acid-acetic.conf

# Local settings. Anything below the source-file line wins.
set -g status-left " #S "
set -g status-right "#[fg=#{@acid_aqua}]#{pane_current_command} "
```

The theme sets colours only: every `*-style` and `*-colour` option that draws
the status line, borders, messages, copy mode, menus and popups. The status
line's content stays yours.

Every role is also a user option, `@acid_<role>`, so a format can name a colour
rather than repeat its value: `#[fg=#{@acid_blue}]`.

Written for tmux 3.8. Every option is set with `-q`, so tmux 3.2 to 3.7 load
it too: each skips the options it does not have, without an error, and draws
the rest.

`window-style` and `window-active-style` are left alone, so panes keep the
terminal's own background. Pair it with the Acid theme for your terminal.

